      "excerpt": "I walked through the places where we used to stay,\nHolding the memories that never fade away.\nI don't know when everything went wrong,",
      "body": "I walked through the places where we used to stay,\nHolding the memories that never fade away.\nI don't know when everything went wrong,\nBut somehow the pain has stayed for so long.\n\nI tried to hide the things I feel inside,\nSmiling with the pain that I always hide.\nMaybe I was scared to make things fall,\nBut in trying to save us, I lost it all.\n\nThe places we knew still carry our name,\nEverything looks same, but nothing feels the same.\nI wish I could turn back the time we had,\nAnd fix every moment that made us sad.\n\nI don't know if my prayers will ever reach you,\nBut I still wish happiness follows you.\nEven if someday we're strangers afar,\nI'll remember the person behind the scar.\n\nMaybe some things are not meant to be fixed,\nMaybe some memories are meant to exist.\nI'll carry the pain and let the time heal,\nSome scars stay forever, but they slowly feel less real.\n\nYou wrote of scars that nobody can see,\nMaybe you don't know, but there's one in me.\nDifferent stories, but somehow we feel the same,\nTwo hearts carrying an invisible pain.\n\nTime:A fortune to pay"
