      "excerpt": "Time moves so fast, yet memories stay,\nTaking the moments we once had away.\nWe thought those little moments would always remain,",
      "body": "Time moves so fast, yet memories stay,\nTaking the moments we once had away.\nWe thought those little moments would always remain,\nBut some beautiful things are followed by pain.\n\nMaybe we fell too deep without knowing the way,\nHolding on to feelings we couldn't explain.\nWe tried to understand, we tried to make it right,\nBut somehow we still lost the beautiful light.\n\nThe memories remain like pictures on a wall,\nThe little things still remind me of it all.\nThe laughter, the talks, the moments we knew,\nSometimes I still miss the person I knew.\n\nMaybe we both changed along the way,\nMaybe some things were never meant to stay.\nBut I don't blame you for the things that went wrong,\nSome feelings are heavy, even when we stay strong.\n\nYou said you tried to warn, you tried to convey,\nMaybe some things just couldn't be changed that day.\nAnd if time was the fortune we had to pay,\nI'd still be grateful for the memories we made.\n\nI don't know what tomorrow has in store,\nOr if we'll ever be the same as before.\nBut whatever happens, wherever we are,\nSome people stay close, even when they're far.\n\nSo don't carry all the blame inside,\nYou don't have to always pretend you're fine.\nSome things hurt, some memories remain,\nBut you don't have to walk through them alone again.\n\nI got everything I wanted"
