      "excerpt": "You said I never chose you, but that's not true,\nMaybe I never showed you what I felt for you.\nBehind every silence, behind every fight,",
      "body": "You said I never chose you, but that's not true,\nMaybe I never showed you what I felt for you.\nBehind every silence, behind every fight,\nYou were the thought that stayed with me every night.\n\nYou wanted to be chosen, you wanted an “us”,\nAnd maybe I made you feel you couldn't trust.\nI told you to stay away, I acted so cold,\nBut there was a reason I never told.\n\nI was afraid of what my feelings could do,\nAfraid that getting closer would only hurt you.\nSo I pushed you away when I wanted you near,\nAnd called it protection when it was really fear.\n\nYou say you gave everything, and I know you did,\nBut I had feelings too, just kept them hid.\nI wanted your time, your smile, your hand,\nI wanted to be beside you, I wanted to understand.\n\nYou think I chose comfort instead of choosing you,\nBut you don't know how many times I wanted to.\nIf choosing you was all that I had to decide,\nI'd choose you again, with nothing to hide.\n\nI never wanted you to learn how to let go,\nOr become unaffected because I hurt you so.\nI don't want your heart to become cold and numb,\nJust because I was afraid of what we could become.\n\nYou mean more to me than these words can explain,\nAnd losing you is something I don't want to name.\nI don't want to promise a perfect road,\nI just want you to know you don't have to carry it alone.\n\nMaybe I've made mistakes, maybe I've made you cry,\nMaybe I pushed you away when I wanted you by my side.\nBut if you ever wonder what my heart chose to do,\nIt chose you, even when I was too afraid to choose you.\n\nLoneliness: An epitome of Mistakes"
