      "excerpt": "Maybe loneliness has followed me too,\nA place where I keep thinking about you.\nI smile with people, I talk and I laugh,",
      "body": "Maybe loneliness has followed me too,\nA place where I keep thinking about you.\nI smile with people, I talk and I laugh,\nBut deep inside, I'm still looking at the past.\n\nI've made my mistakes, I've carried my pain,\nTried to hide everything again and again.\nSometimes I wonder if I'm really okay,\nOr just pretending to be fine every day.\n\nI know that feeling when the silence gets loud,\nWhen you're surrounded but still lost in the crowd.\nWhen your own thoughts become hard to escape,\nAnd every little memory takes its shape.\n\nI've walked through the darkness you wrote about,\nWith questions inside that I can't figure out.\nI've tried to understand where everything went wrong,\nWhile pretending to myself that I could stay strong.\n\nMaybe we both have our own mistakes to carry,\nOur own little battles that make our hearts weary.\nMaybe we both lost things we wanted to keep,\nAnd buried our feelings somewhere too deep.\n\nYou called loneliness an epitome of mistakes,\nMaybe I know the same road that your heart takes.\nI don't have an answer, I don't know the way,\nI'm just feeling the same things you couldn't say.\n\nAnd maybe that's why your words hurt me too,\nBecause somewhere in them, I found myself with you.\nDifferent stories, different wounds, different nights,\nBut somehow the same darkness under different lights.\n\nSo I won't tell you that everything will be fine,\nBecause I'm still trying to figure out mine.\nI just wanted you to know, if you ever feel alone,\nMaybe I'm somewhere feeling the same on my own."
